  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "previous-orphan",
      "status": "addressed",
      "detail": "Queue handlers signal only the observer and await close; the observer installs cancellation before app spawn and always enters owned-process cleanup on the exercised startup, inspector and measurement cancellation paths. Known identities survive reparenting; exact fixture markers also find independently reparented helper/Crashpad processes. Persistence failure cannot bypass the exercised cleanup path."
    },
    {
      "id": "boundary-and-continuous-isolation",
      "status": "addressed",
      "detail": "The runner inventories before launch, every 5 seconds and after observer close. Verification rejects any DesMon at boundaries, missing measured main during observation, unexpected identities, missing ownership, changed PID/start identity, over-10-second gaps including between slots, or incomplete/cancelled lifecycle. Process identity is linked to every raw metrics Browser PID/creationTime."
    },
    {
      "id": "binding-and-independent-acceptance",
      "status": "addressed",
      "detail": "Five exact slots bind prospective registration, reviewer, current source, observers, protocol, apps, reports, lifecycle and raw inventories. Final acceptance requires numerical verification, isolation replay and a later current-source result review from the registered reviewer; Root and Designer cannot approve their own performance infrastructure. Numeric pass alone no longer authorizes completion."
    },
    {
      "id": "existing-failure-history",
      "status": "preserved",
      "detail": "The earlier method approval and changes-required result review remain unchanged. matched03 numeric results do not regain isolation acceptance through this code review."
    }
  ],
  "remainingLimitations": [
    "Sampling does not prove absence of processes whose complete lifetime lies between inventories. The guard explicitly accepts at most 10 seconds between sampled observations; this is sampled evidence, not continuous OS tracing.",
    "The inventory targets DesMon executables and unique performance-fixture markers. Arbitrary Electron/Node builds, simulations or other resource-heavy work are not inferred from these rows. The next prospective registration and work journal must prohibit agent concurrency; ordinary user applications remain uncontrolled ambient conditions.",
    "Full command line matching can fail closed on unrelated command text containing the specific marker. The isolation guard does not kill unrelated or user-owned applications.",
    "Identity revalidation immediately before each signal narrows PID reuse races but cannot provide a portable atomic process handle on macOS. OS SIGKILL/crash/power loss can still bypass application cleanup; leftover identities must make the next registered boundary fail.",
    "The 5-second ps inventory adds observation overhead to both versions. Its unchanged cadence and equal treatment must remain prospectively bound.",
    "The two 30-second normal-completion preflights validate lifecycle/guard compatibility only. They satisfy neither 30/180-minute durations nor numerical performance acceptance.",
    "Future registration must fix one whole five-slot block, unchanged budgets/formulas and selection rules before new baseline results are seen. No future performance acceptance is issued here."
  ],
